# MQ02 "Deliver the Amulet". Charactergen 88 started it at stage 20 (task: take the Amulet of Kings to Jauffre at
# Weynon Priory). MQ02Script polls: stage 30 when the player stands in the Chorrol exterior cell, stage 40 in the
# WeynonPriory exterior cell (both only while OUTSIDE). Jauffre's topic chain then ends in "Where can I find Uriel's
# son?", which sets MQ02 50 (-> 100) and starts MQ03 (stage 10).
# The ride from the sewer exit to Chorrol and the priory is the player's walk; coc into the exterior cells stands in
# for it (the cells are the TES4 EditorIDs Chorrol and WeynonPriory).

case mq02_chorrol
expect GetStageDone MQ02 20
run
coc Chorrol
wait 90
until 600 GetStageDone MQ02 30
end

case mq02_weynon_priory_exterior
run
coc WeynonPriory
wait 90
until 600 GetStageDone MQ02 40
end

# The player goes into the priory house, where Jauffre is (JauffreRef, WeynonPrioryHouse). Brother Piner / Prior
# Maborel (stage 42) are optional and not visited.
case mq02_enter_priory_house
run
coc WeynonPrioryHouse
wait 90
expect player.GetInCell WeynonPrioryHouse
end

# Jauffre's greeting offers "I brought you the Amulet of Kings." (MQ02JauffreA1). Each answer leads to the next topic:
# A1 -> B1 "[Give Jauffre the Amulet]" (takes the amulet) -> C1 -> D1 -> D4 -> D3 -> E1.
case mq02_give_amulet
talk Jauffre
ask "I brought you the Amulet of Kings."
ask "[Give Jauffre the Amulet]"
expect player.GetItemCount AmuletofKings == 0
ask "Tell the emperor's last words."
ask "Who is the Prince of Destruction?"
ask "How can Oblivion threaten us, then?"
ask "The Emperor asked me to find his son."
ask "Where can I find Uriel's son?"
bye
until 300 GetStageDone MQ02 50
until 300 GetStageDone MQ02 100
expect GetStageDone MQ03 10
end
